# Enums and metrics

WorkItem enums must match API and UI:

- kind: `Incident` | `Issue` | `Task`
- priority: `none` | `low` | `medium` | `high` | `urgent`
- role: `Developer` | `infra` | `SA` | null (functional work role, not permission)
- status: `backlog` | `todo` | `in-progress` | `blocked` | `sa-testing` | `pm-testing` | `completed` | `cancelled`

Serialize Prisma underscores to hyphenated public status: `in_progress` ↔ `in-progress`, `sa_testing` ↔ `sa-testing`, `pm_testing` ↔ `pm-testing`.

One formula everywhere:

- Total = WorkItems matching filters (all statuses)
- Open = not `completed` and not `cancelled`
- Completed = `status = completed` only — never include `cancelled`
- Completion rate and Project progress = completed ÷ (total − cancelled) × 100; denominator 0 → 0%
- Overdue = `dueDate` before today in Asia/Bangkok and status not completed/cancelled
- Logged hours = SUM(`TimeEntry.hours`) for the range/filters; keep decimals; do not round before the sum
- Work Items list group "Complete" may include `cancelled`; metric labels must stay distinct
- `submittedAt` is stamped for `sa-testing` or `completed` — it is not `completedAt`
- Do not chart historical throughput from current status. Add `completedAt` or status history first
- Project status comments: Planning / In Progress / Review / Completed / On Hold. Priority: Low / Medium / High / Critical
